      (:code "(define (as-ratio a b) (exact/rat a b))\n(exact/->string (as-ratio 7 22))" :tags (math program))
      (:code "(define (build-fraction n d) (if (and (integer? n) (integer? d) (not (zero? d))) (exact/rat n d) (error 'shape 'bad-fraction)))\n(build-fraction 3 4)" :tags (cs program)))
     :problem "Dollar amounts must be represented as exact rationals for reconciliation; the constructor is the only safe entry point."
     :explanation "eng: money construction. math: ratio construction. cs: guarded builder."
     :meta "Reach for exact/rat and NOT /: / with two integers may go inexact.")
